course: dictionary
lesson: 12627
title: The word dismissal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dismissal comes from the verb dismiss, which means to send someone away or let them go. A dismissal is the act of doing that. The words around it tell you which meaning fits. «Dismissal is at 3 o'clock» means the children are let go from school at the end of the day.
explain: At work, dismissal means losing your job. «Her dismissal from the shop came as a shock, because she had worked there for years.» The words job and worked there show that dismissal means being sacked or fired.
explain: Dismissal can also mean refusing to take an idea seriously, or a judge stopping a court case. «His dismissal of my plan hurt my feelings» means he did not take my plan seriously. Try swapping in another word, such as rejection, to check if it still makes sense.
fact: Dismissal is a noun, and it comes from the verb dismiss.
fact: «Dismissal» can mean the time children leave school, as in «school dismissal» or «early dismissal».
fact: At work, «dismissal» means being sacked or fired, as in «unfair dismissal».
fact: In a court, a «dismissal of a case» means the judge decides the case will not go on.
fact: In cricket, a dismissal means a batter is out.
exercise: «Dismissal is at 3 o'clock.» What does dismissal mean here? | A lesson about shapes | The start of the summer holidays | A test that children must sit | *The time children are let go from school
exercise: «Her dismissal from the shop came as a shock.» What does dismissal mean? | Being given a bonus for good work | Going on a holiday | Winning a prize at the shop | *Being sacked from her job
exercise: Which sentence uses dismissal to mean refusing to take an idea seriously? | The class had an early dismissal today | *His dismissal of my idea made me feel small | The batter had a dismissal in the first over | The judge gave a dismissal of the case
test: «The team faced unfair dismissal after the manager's decision.» What is the best meaning of dismissal here? | A short break from work | Being let out of school early | *Being sacked from a job, unfairly | Being given extra time to finish
test: Which of these is a good swap for dismissal when it means letting people go at the end of the school day? | A long holiday | A school trip | A spelling test | *Going home time
exam: «The judge's dismissal of the case meant the trial was over.» What does dismissal mean here? | *A decision that the case will not go on | A letter asking someone to come to court | A prize given to the winning side | A long wait before the trial starts
